# The function bundle is chosen by `includeFiles` in vercel.json; this keeps the
# *upload* small and, more importantly, keeps two things off Vercel entirely.
#
# `var/` is the local SQLite database and Chroma index — a session's documents and
# every step of its trace. It has no business leaving this machine, and the
# deployment does not read it: `api/index.py` runs on `:memory:`.
var/
.env
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
tests/
reference/
docs/

# **Kept out so `requirements.txt` is the one that is read.** Vercel's Python
# runtime prefers `pyproject.toml` when both are present, and it installs only
# `[project] dependencies` from it — the `parsers` and `vector` extras are optional
# by design, so the bundle came up without openpyxl, pypdf and the rest, and
# `load_golden_set()` died on `from openpyxl import Workbook` the first time the
# Why-agentic page asked for the pain points. Locally nothing changes: development
# still installs `pip install -e ".[dev,vector,parsers]"` from this file.
pyproject.toml
